"""English stimulus scripts, v2. kind: 'speech' = examiner voice with the real content of the task (40-60 s);
'instr' = short spoken instruction, the task itself is on screen (video) and silent; 'tones' = instruction + tone sequence.
Instr/tones audio is padded with near-silence to the video length, as the real task sounds."""
import sys
sys.path.insert(0, "./backend")
from es_core.stories import STORIES
STORY = STORIES["lantern-keeper-en"].text
S = {
"story_retell": ("speech", "You will hear a short story. Listen carefully, and then retell it in your own words, as many details as you remember. Here is the story. " + STORY),
"picture_description": ("speech", "Look at the picture on the screen. It shows a street scene on a rainy afternoon, with several people, a dog, and a bus. Describe aloud what you see in the picture. Say who is there, what each person is doing, what the weather is like, and what is happening around them. Speak in full sentences and take your time. Then tell me what you think may happen next. If you notice something unusual or funny in the picture, mention it too. You can describe the details on the left, on the right, and in the middle. When you have finished, say that you are done. Now look at the second picture, a backyard on a windy day, and describe it in the same way."),
"naming_fluency": ("speech", "Name as many animals as you can in one minute. Any animals, wild or domestic, big or small. Do not repeat the same animal twice. Start when you hear the beep. Here is an example of how it sounds. Cat, horse, elephant, sparrow, crocodile, rabbit, giraffe, salmon, spider, camel, wolf, dolphin, hedgehog, tiger, goat, penguin, bee, cow, kangaroo, owl. Keep going until the time is up. Think of animals in the forest, on the farm, in the sea, in the desert, and in the sky. Ready? Time starts now."),
"word_list_recall_spoken": ("speech", "I am going to say six words. Remember them, because I will ask you to repeat them. Listen. Apple. Table. River. Lamp. Dog. Cloud. Once again. Apple. Table. River. Lamp. Dog. Cloud. Now, repeat aloud all the words you remember, in any order. Take your time. Think about the list I read. It started with a fruit and ended with something in the sky. Say every word that comes to mind. If you cannot remember all of them, that is fine. Say the ones you remember. Now say the words you remember."),
"naming_from_definition": ("speech", "I will describe an object, and you name it with one word. Listen. You write on paper with it. It has a thin core inside, and you hold it in your hand. What is it called? Next object. It hangs on the wall. It shows the time and it has two hands. What is it called? Next object. You open it with a key, and people walk through it to enter a room or a house. What is it called? Next. It is a yellow fruit with a thick peel, and monkeys like it. What is it called? Next. You wear it on your head when it is cold, and it is often made of wool. What is it called? Say the word aloud after each description."),
"picture_naming": ("speech", "A picture will appear on the screen. Name the object that is drawn on it, aloud, with one word. First picture. What is it? Second picture. What is it? Third picture. Name the object. Fourth picture. What do you see? Fifth picture. Say what it is. Sixth picture. What is this called? Take your time, but try to answer before the next picture appears. If you cannot find the word, you can describe what the object is used for, or say what it looks like. Seventh picture. Name it aloud. Eighth picture. What is it? Last picture. Name the object."),
"sentence_completion_spoken": ("speech", "I will begin a sentence, and you finish it aloud with any words that fit. In the morning I usually drink. When it is cold outside, I put on. In the shop I bought some bread and. In the evening the whole family sits down at. On Sunday we like to go to. My favorite food is. When I cannot sleep, I. The weather today is. At the market you can buy. When the phone rings, I. Finish every sentence in your own way. There are no wrong answers. Say the whole sentence if you like. Here is the next one. After lunch I often."),
"describe_daily_routine": ("speech", "Tell me about your usual day. When do you get up, what do you do in the morning, what are you busy with in the afternoon, and how do you spend the evening? Speak slowly, in detail, in full sentences. You can say what you eat for breakfast, where you go, whom you meet, and what you like best about the day. You can also tell me about the weekend, and how it is different from a weekday. If you remember something funny or pleasant that happened recently, tell me about it. Take your time. I am listening. Begin when you are ready, and speak for about a minute."),
"read_aloud_short_text": ("speech", "Read the short text on the screen aloud. Read slowly and clearly. Here it is. In autumn the days get shorter. Yellow leaves fall from the trees, and in the morning a thin fog stands over the river. People take out their warm jackets and drink tea with honey. Children walk to school with bright umbrellas, and the old man in the park feeds the ducks with bread. In the evening the lamps come on early, and the windows glow warm and yellow. Smoke rises from the chimneys, and the smell of fresh bread comes from the small bakery on the corner. Now read the text aloud. Take your time and say each word clearly."),
"sentence_building_cards": ("instr", "You see cards with words. Build a correct sentence by dragging the cards in order. When the sentence is ready, press the Done button. You can move the cards as many times as you need."),
"word_picture_matching": ("speech", "You will hear a word. Choose the picture that matches it. Listen. The word is cup. Now choose the picture. The word is tree. Choose the picture. The word is bus. Choose the picture. The word is key. Choose the picture. The word is bread. Choose the picture. The word is lamp. Choose the picture. The word is bird. Choose the picture. The word is house. Choose the picture. The word is clock. Choose the picture. The word is apple. Choose the picture. Tap the picture you think is right and wait for the next word. The last word is dog. Choose the picture."),
"sound_to_picture": ("tones", "You will hear a sound. Choose the picture that matches it. Listen."),
"odd_one_out": ("instr", "There are four pictures on the screen. Three of them are alike in meaning, and one does not belong. Find the odd one out and tap it. For example, three fruits and one tool."),
"picture_pair_memory": ("instr", "Cards are lying face down on the screen. Turn over two cards at a time and look for identical pictures. Pairs you find stay open. Remember where each picture is."),
"spatial_sequence_recall": ("instr", "Squares on the board light up one by one. Remember the order. When the lights stop, tap the squares in the same order. The sequence may get a little longer each time."),
"delayed_picture_recognition": ("instr", "A few minutes ago you saw a set of pictures. Now you will be shown pictures one at a time. Tap Yes if the picture was in the set, and No if it is new."),
"route_recall_map": ("instr", "The map shows a route from home to the shop. Look at the route and remember the turns. Then the map will disappear, and you will mark the same route on it."),
"face_name_choice": ("instr", "You will see a person's face and several names. Choose the name you saw earlier next to this face. If you do not remember, choose the most fitting one."),
"shopping_list_recall_visual": ("instr", "You will see pictures of items from a shopping list. Remember them. Then select on the screen only the items that were on the list."),
"digit_span_tap": ("instr", "Digits will appear on the screen one after another. Remember their order. Then tap the same digits in the same order on the keypad."),
"spot_the_difference": ("instr", "You see two almost identical pictures. Find five differences and tap each one. The number of differences found is shown at the top."),
"sustained_tone_detection": ("tones", "You will listen to a steady beep. Sometimes it will be different, a little higher. As soon as you notice the different beep, press the button. Listen carefully."),
"card_sorting": ("instr", "Sort the cards into groups by the rule. First by color. The rule may change, and then you sort by shape. Watch the hint on the screen."),
"rhythm_copy": ("tones", "You will hear a rhythm of short beats. Listen to it, and then repeat it by tapping in the same rhythm. Listen."),
"reaction_tap": ("instr", "Circles will appear on the screen. As soon as a green circle appears, tap it quickly. Do not tap the red circles."),
}
TEXT_IDS = ["story_retell","picture_description","naming_fluency","word_list_recall_spoken","naming_from_definition",
            "picture_naming","sentence_completion_spoken","describe_daily_routine","read_aloud_short_text","word_picture_matching"]
